s\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786571503069597001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6aee3269-2145-4179-a7ad-0b6a4fa46c3d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b902-18af-14ed-4da1"},{"link_uuid":"76577685-b550-4958-9600-f6f42560e4a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a061-50fb-928f-49b4"}],"description":"Operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 breaking pass #3), 2026-08-12. Source: the DEPRECATION REMOVAL-READINESS SURVEY, comment #11 on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (b902-18af-14ed-4da1), Tier 2 item 3. Operator ruling (verbatim): \"The two best candidates and the one ready now are all approved for removal.\" Third and last change of the pass, after checked-unhelpful-tanager and priceless-charred-fruitbat.\n\n## What\n\nRemove the deprecated bare env var `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` (deprecated 1fbfb5c691, shipped v0.11.0; ADR 0057). The per-class `[tool.rebar.llm.model_classes]` slots are the interface; the bare scalar is a SUPERSESSION with a migration window that the operator has now closed early.\n\n## SCOPE NARROWING — the config key `[tool.rebar.llm].model` STAYS\n\nThe survey framed this as \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL / llm.model\". Evidence says only the ENV VAR is removable, and that matches the registry, whose single row (`src/rebar/_deprecations.py:101`) is env-only:\n\n- `rebar.toml` sets `[tool.rebar.llm].model` deliberately and load-bearingly (it pins the provider so provider inference cannot leak to a non-Bedrock default).\n- `LLMConfig.model` is read widely across the runtime and is the value model-class resolution falls back to.\n- `docs/config.md:320` documents `model` as a live key; only its \"env `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`\" annotation goes.\n\nSo this ticket removes ONE env channel and leaves the config key, the CLI `-c llm.model` override, and the per-step `model:` workflow override untouched.\n\n## Scope (current main)\n\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:92-101` — delete the `_scheduled(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL\", …)` row and its explanatory comment block; append this removal to the historical-record NOTE.\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:~249` — ADD the tombstone `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL\", \"the [tool.rebar.llm.model_classes] slots\", \"error\")`, directly mirroring the `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` row at :249.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:529-536` — wire the new tombstone check next to the existing `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` check in `LLMConfig.from_env`, the same fail-loud placement (a retired LLM knob fails only when the LLM stack loads; `RemovedInputError` is a `BaseException` so the broad `except Exception` in this method cannot swallow it).\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:581-597` — delete the warn-when-set block; `:599` — stop reading the env for `model`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:373` — `_llm_str` gains `env_name: str | None`, skipping the env read when `None`, so `model` resolves CLI > config table > default with no env channel.\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:230-250` — delete `_deprecated_bare_model()`; drop the `fallback_default` rung so class precedence becomes CLI > per-class env > config table > built-in default (`:183-189` comment updated).\n\n### Prose/comment sites in `src/` that name the variable (all must move, or AC-1 cannot pass)\n\n`src/rebar/llm/config.py:10` (module env table), `:285` (the `resolve_model` docstring describing `cfg.model` as folding the env read — FACTUALLY FALSE post-removal), `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:70` (says a non-default `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` still wins — also FACTUALLY FALSE post-removal), `src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py:14` (a historical sizing anecdote; reword to past tense, it is a record of why a change was unlandable).\n\n### Test consumers (the blocking risk: they set the env and go through `LLMConfig.from_env`)\n\nAfter the tombstone lands, ANY test that sets `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` and builds an `LLMConfig` will RAISE `RemovedInputError` instead of resolving. All 15 files that reference the variable must be retargeted to `[tool.rebar.llm].model`, a per-class `REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_MODEL`, or the `-c llm.model` override: `tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py` (retargeted to assert the fail-loud tombstone), `test_config_llm.py`, `test_ci_provider_matrix.py`, `test_llm_config_pointer.py`, `test_project_default_provider.py`, `test_llm_config_gate_root.py`, `test_gate_context_seam.py`, `test_bedrock_provider.py`, `test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py`, `test_code_review_per_pass_classes.py`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_code_review_usage_attribution.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_scoped_ticket_tool.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`.\n\n### `infra/` (operator-facing, hand-written)\n\n`infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:334-339` tells operators not to reach for the alias and names `model_classes._deprecated_bare_model`, a symbol this change deletes; `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:170-178` explains why the variable is deliberately not set. Both are reworded to \"removed\", not \"deprecated\".\n\n## Registry/tombstone treatment (mirrors precedent)\n\nDeleted row + historical NOTE is the DE7 / ticket-5899 shape. UNLIKE removal #2, this one DOES take a tombstone: the tombstone registry covers `env`/`cfg`/`file` inputs, and the closest precedent — `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS\", \"REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS\", \"error\")`, also a superseded LLM knob checked in `llm.config.from_env` — is `behavior=\"error\"`. Fail-loud is right here because silently ignoring a still-set `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` would quietly change which model every operation runs, i.e. cost and quality, with no signal. Record \"operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 pass #3), 2026-08-12\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The env var is gone from the resolver and from every prose site that described it as live; checked: `grep -rn REBAR_LLM_MODEL src/rebar` matches ONLY the tombstone row in `_deprecations.py`, its `from_env` check, and the historical-record NOTE (a raw grep, since env names are string literals the LSP cannot resolve).\n- [ ] A still-set `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` FAILS LOUD with the migration message rather than being ignored; checked: `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=x rebar review-plan --check` exits non-zero naming the model_classes slots.\n- [ ] `[tool.rebar.llm].model`, `-c llm.model` and the per-step `model:` override all still resolve; proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_config_llm.py`.\n- [ ] The deprecation row is deleted and the tombstone added; proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is REGENERATED, not hand-edited, and no longer lists the variable; checked: `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && git diff --exit-code docs/env-vars.md`.\n- [ ] Hand-written docs and operator material drop the variable: `docs/config.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, `docs/local-dev-env.md`, `docs/ci-provider-matrix.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md`, `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`. ADR 0057 stays as historical record.\n- [ ] No test sets the removed env and then builds an `LLMConfig` (which would now raise); proven by the full `pytest` suite passing.\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` record the removal in the prior passes' table format.\n- [ ] Gates green; checked: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — the commit gate.\n- `pytest` (full suite); `tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py` covers the deprecation being removed and is retargeted to the tombstone's fail-loud behaviour.\n- `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && git diff --exit-code docs/env-vars.md` — the CI env-registry drift gate.\n- `grep -rn REBAR_LLM_MODEL src tests docs infra` — raw grep for the string-literal env name, including the operator-facing `infra/` runbook and compose file.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"delete the scheduled env row, add the fail-loud tombstone, record the pass in the historical NOTE"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"wire the tombstone check, delete the warn block, drop the env channel from the model resolver, allow _llm_str env_name=None"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"delete _deprecated_bare_model and the fallback_default rung"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"drop the env annotation from the model key"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"drop the deprecated env from the precedence prose and env table"},{"path":"docs/llm-example-configs.md","reason":"drop the deprecated env from the precedence prose"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"drop the do-not-use note for a variable that no longer exists"},{"path":"docs/ci-provider-matrix.md","reason":"drop the not-used-here section for a removed variable"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"drop the env from the model-override note"},{"path":"docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md","reason":"drop the env from the precedence chain"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"BREAKING (pre-1.0) entry for pass #3"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"user-facing removal entry"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py","reason":"retarget from deprecation-warning behaviour to the tombstone fail-loud behaviour"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_llm.py","reason":"drop env-channel cases; keep config-key and CLI resolution"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py","reason":"drop the removed env from the matrix assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_default_provider.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_context_seam.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_per_pass_classes.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_code_review_usage_attribution.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_scoped_ticket_tool.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py","reason":"retarget env usage"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"operator runbook names the removed alias and the deleted _deprecated_bare_model symbol"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"compose comments explain why the removed variable is not set"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"comment claims a non-default REBAR_LLM_MODEL still wins; false post-removal"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py","reason":"historical sizing anecdote naming the alias; reword to past tense"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py","reason":"the deprecation suite renamed from test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py and rewritten as a tombstone suite"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","a061-50fb-928f-49b4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1f8b005b-3768-4cbc-a864-c70d40e1fa93","plan_review_phase":"execution","pre